  "id": "habit-formation",
  "term": "habit formation",
  "definition": "Habit formation is the process by which a behavior becomes an automatic response to cues in the surrounding context. It is encouraged by repeating the behavior in a stable setting, and perceived reward may also play a role in how this process develops.",
